# Review: Feed

The spec is a new design, and the code does not implement it yet. The six `FeedStore` ops that
already exist (`append`, `appendLocal`, `query`, `subscribe`, `countBlocks`, `deleteOldestBlocks`)
are present and tested. The four new ops are not: `setFeedOptions`, `getFeedOptions`, `trim` and
`trimAll` exist nowhere in `dxos` or `edge`. No migration adds `feeds.options` or the
`idx_blocks_feedPrivateId_timestamp` index; the latest migration is
`0004_sync_state_blocks_to_pull.sql`. `append` and `appendLocal` do not trim, and `query` and
`subscribe` do not filter by age. The upstream side is missing too: `Feed.RetentionOptions` in
`@dxos/echo` holds only `cursor`, and `Feed.setRetention` is a no-op.

The only retention in the code today is on EDGE. `FeedSpace._trimFeedIfNeeded` caps trace-namespace
feeds at `config.queues.maxTraceQueueItems` (default 1000) using `countBlocks` and
`deleteOldestBlocks`. It runs from the notification-queue alarm, after the append has committed, not
in the same transaction, and it has no bound per call. This is the base that F-2.6 builds on.

Of 17 items: 0 done, 0 untested, 3 partial, 0 diverged, 14 missing. Three findings matter most:

- **No options storage at all.** F-1 depends on a column, a migration and two ops that do not exist,
  and the `Feed` object on the echo side carries neither `maxLength` nor `maxAge`.
- **No transactional trim.** `deleteOldestBlocks` deletes by `insertionId` in its own statement and
  has no `TRIM_LIMIT` bound and no `more` signal, so F-2.1, F-2.4, F-2.7 and F-2.8 have nothing to
  build on beyond that primitive.
- **EDGE trims out of band.** The trace cap runs on the alarm, after the append commits, so even
  F-2.6's existing half does not match F-2.1's "in the same transaction".

