```mdl
verdict FeedStore: The six existing ops are present and tested; the four new ops are missing, and the existing ones neither trim nor hide.
  status: partial
  evidence:
    [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore.append,
     github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore.appendLocal,
     github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore.query,
     github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore.subscribe,
     github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore.countBlocks,
     github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.ts#FeedStore.deleteOldestBlocks]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/feed-store.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/feed/src/sync.test.ts]
  note: |
    `append`, `appendLocal`, `query`, `subscribe`, `countBlocks` and `deleteOldestBlocks` exist on `FeedStore` as
    Effects that require `SqlClient`; `feed-store.test.ts` exercises all six (`countBlocks` and `deleteOldestBlocks`
    in the two tests near L578-700). The ops take an options bag (`{ spaceId, feedNamespace, feedId }`), not a
    `FeedKey` type, which the spec's note describes informally. Missing: `setFeedOptions`, `getFeedOptions`, `trim`,
    `trimAll`, `TrimResult` and `TRIM_LIMIT`, which appear nowhere in the dxos or edge repos. The annotations on the
    existing ops are not met: `append` and `appendLocal` do not trim after insert (`appendLocal` carries a TODO for
    retention), and `query` and `subscribe` do not hide blocks past `maxAge`.
```

```mdl
verdict F-1.1: There is no setFeedOptions or getFeedOptions, and no migration adds feeds.options.
  status: missing
  note: |
    Searched `packages/` in dxos and edge for `setFeedOptions`, `getFeedOptions` and `FeedOptions`: no matches (only the
    unrelated `AppendToAgentFeedOptions` on EDGE). `src/migrations/0001_init.sql` defines `feeds` with `feedPrivateId`,
    `spaceId`, `feedId` and `feedNamespace` only, and 0002-0004 alter `blocks` and `sync_state`, never `feeds`.
    `#ensureFeed` creates a feed row only on the first append, so a row for a feed with no blocks has no creation path
    yet.
```

