```mdl
verdict F-2.1: No per-feed maxLength; nothing trims after append, pull or options apply on the device store.
  status: missing
  note: |
    `FeedStore.append` and `FeedStore.appendLocal` insert and return without any trim, and there is no
    `retention.maxLength` to read. The closest code is EDGE's trace cap (`FeedSpace._trimFeedIfNeeded`), which uses the
    host's config, not a feed's option, and runs from the notification-queue alarm after the append has committed, not
    in the same transaction. `deleteOldestBlocks` is the primitive a trim would call.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.2: No maxAge: query and subscribe return every block, and nothing deletes by age.
  status: missing
  note: |
    `FeedStore.query` and `FeedStore.subscribe` filter by feed, position and cursor only, never by `timestamp`. No
    `trimAll` runs at store open or on the FeedSpace alarm, and there is no `idx_blocks_feedPrivateId_timestamp`
    index in `src/migrations/`. `blocks.timestamp` exists (0001_init.sql), so the column the filter needs is present.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.3: Neither limit exists, so their combination does not either.
  status: missing
  note: No `trim` op and no `maxLength` or `maxAge` in the store or in `Feed.RetentionOptions` (which holds only `cursor`).
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.4: A sync pull inserts every block it receives; nothing drops them in that transaction.
  status: missing
  note: |
    `FeedStore.append` (the pull path, via `sync-client.ts`) runs `#insertSealed` in one transaction with no
    retention step, and `recordPullProgress` advances the pull position independently of any trim. Nothing keeps a
    dropped block from being requested again because nothing drops one.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.5: There is no retention to delete live-object blocks, so the rule is not implemented.
  status: missing
  note: |
    No retention exists to apply the rule to. The existing primitive already has the stated property:
    `deleteOldestBlocks` deletes by `insertionId` order with no regard to object ids or superseded versions. The rule
    says "by position"; `deleteOldestBlocks` orders by `insertionId`, which differs from `position` on a replica, so
    `trim` should state which order it uses.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.6: EDGE caps trace feeds at maxTraceQueueItems, but no feed option can lower that cap.
  status: partial
  evidence:
    [github:dxos/edge/packages/services/db-service/src/worker/feed-space/feed-space.ts#FeedSpace._getMaxQueueSize,
     github:dxos/edge/packages/services/db-service/src/worker/feed-space/feed-space.ts#FeedSpace._trimFeedIfNeeded,
     github:dxos/edge/packages/services/db-service/src/worker/feed-space/feed-space.ts#DEFAULT_TRACE_QUEUE_MAX_SIZE]
  tests: [github:dxos/edge/packages/services/db-service/test/feed-space.workerd.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The cap is maxTraceQueueItems for the trace namespace, falling back to 1000, and undefined otherwise. github:dxos/edge/packages/services/db-service/src/worker/feed-space/feed-space.ts#FeedSpace._getMaxQueueSize
    - After each queued append notification, the alarm counts the feed's blocks and deletes the excess oldest ones. github:dxos/edge/packages/services/db-service/src/worker/feed-space/feed-space.ts#FeedSpace._trimFeedIfNeeded
  note: |
    Done: the "with no maxLength" clause. `_getMaxQueueSize` applies `config.queues.maxTraceQueueItems` (default
    `DEFAULT_TRACE_QUEUE_MAX_SIZE = 1000`), and the workerd test "trace namespace keeps only the latest entries" checks
    it. Missing: there are no stored options, so the limit is never `min(retention.maxLength, maxTraceQueueItems)`.
    The trim also runs in its own statements from the alarm and deletes the whole excess in one call, unbounded.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.7: There is no trim or trimAll, no TRIM_LIMIT and no more flag.
  status: missing
  note: |
    `deleteOldestBlocks` takes a caller-chosen `count`, deletes oldest first by `insertionId`, and returns the number
    deleted; it has no 10,000 cap and no `more` result. EDGE's `_trimFeedIfNeeded` passes the whole excess as `count`,
    so a large first trim is unbounded in one call. No EchoHost or FeedSpace loop repeats a trim.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.8: No trim exists to be idempotent or safe under concurrency.
  status: missing
  note: |
    No `trim` op. `deleteOldestBlocks` is not idempotent by itself (it deletes `count` more blocks on every call); the
    convergence the requirement describes must come from `trim` computing the excess from the limits each time.
```

```mdl
verdict T-1: No test applies retention { maxLength: 5 } and checks that only 5 blocks remain.
  status: missing
  note: |
    `feed-store.test.ts` tests `countBlocks` and `deleteOldestBlocks` with an explicit count, which is not retention by
    options. EDGE's trace-trim workerd test is the closest, but uses the host config, not a feed's `maxLength`.
```

